    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0178" n="1012" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1012"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112Sa/90</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-29T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 29, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3114. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1737. Embassy’s 2865, October 16, 8 p.m., your 1683. Plan suggested does not
                    meet with the approval of the Department. We <pb facs="0179" n="1013"
                        xml:id="pg1013"/> are now in consultation with Department with view to
                    preparing a revised plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
